    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on attacking favorable matchups against mid-tier arms, headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (72.63) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19). **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, benefiting from a high-run-environment park and a premium #3 slot against Eury P\u00e9rez. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** draws a high-upside matchup against the southpaw Lodolo; despite the L/L dynamic, his projection holds firm due to his favorable placement in the heart of the order. **Bryson Stott** (71.23) also grades out as a \"Strong\" play, buoyed by a generous 5.01 xERA matchup against Avila, though we are monitoring his stolen base opportunities, as his efficiency score is slightly dampened by the risk of high-intensity holds on the basepaths.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary driver for our mid-tier scoring today. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.67) and **Luis Arraez** (63.97) anchor our infield efficiency, with both maximizing their splits against right-handed pitching. **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.69) is particularly intriguing today; while he is currently listed with a pending lineup, his projected #5 spot against Gordon provides significant value, compounded by the 100% stolen base expectation we\u2019ve modeled against this specific delivery profile. We remain cautious with **Jeremiah Jackson** (56.20), whose score remains marginal due to an unfavorable #8 spot in the order, and we are tracking **Daulton Varsho** (53.14) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (59.18) closely, as their value is highly dependent on official lineup confirmation.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets** (48.63), who fell just shy of the threshold. While **Gavin Sheets** profiles well against right-handed pitching, his projected #4 slot was offset by a challenging matchup against Emmet Sheehan, whose 3.62 xERA suppresses the raw output too significantly to justify displacing our currently slated starters. We are also maintaining standard operating procedure regarding the injured **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined, ensuring our game caps are preserved for active contributors like **Cal Raleigh**, **Masyn Winn**, **Drew Gilbert**, and the rest of the daily squad. Keep a sharp eye on the late-breaking lineup news for those pending slots to ensure no late scratches jeopardize our aggregate efficiency.",
